diff --git a/samples/subsys/mp/multicore/README.rst b/samples/subsys/mp/multicore/README.rst
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..e298c963d06
--- /dev/null
+++ b/samples/subsys/mp/multicore/README.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+.. zephyr:code-sample:: mp-multicore-mjpeg-decode
+   :name: Multicore MJPEG file decode pipeline
+
+Description
+***********
+
+This sample demonstrates a multicore pipeline where the primary core reads an MJPEG file, parses
+it into individual JPEG frames, forwards those frames to a remote JPEG decoder running on a
+secondary core through the ``mp_zvid_transform_client`` element and finally display them on screen.
+
+Pipeline topology
+=================
+
+::
+
+    +----------+     +-------------+     +-------------+     +-------------------+     +-----------------+     +--------------+
+    | file_src | --> | jpeg_parser | --> | capsfilter  | --> | transform_client  | --> | video transform | --> | display sink |
+    +----------+     +-------------+     +-------------+     +-------------------+     +-----------------+     +--------------+
+
+The sample expects an MJPEG file at the path specified by :kconfig:option:`CONFIG_FILE_INPUT_PATH`
+(default ``/SD:/test.mjpeg``). This file is generated at build time using GStreamer CLI, embedded
+into the application as ``mjpeg.inc``, and written to the mounted FAT filesystem automatically on
+first run if it does not already exist.
+
+Requirements
+************
+
+Hardware
+========
+
+This sample currently supports :zephyr:board:`mimxrt1170_evk` using the CM7 as the
+primary core and the CM4 as the remote decode core.
+
+A compatible display shield must be connected for rendering, for example:
+
+- ``rk055hdmipi4ma0``
+
+The sample also requires a writable FAT-formatted SD card because the MJPEG input
+stream is read from the filesystem.
+
+Host tools
+==========
+
+The build host must have GStreamer installed, specifically ``gst-launch-1.0`` and
+the plugins that provide ``videotestsrc`` and ``jpegenc``.
+
+On Debian/Ubuntu::
+
+  sudo apt install gstreamer1.0-tools gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
+
+On Fedora::
+
+  sudo dnf install gstreamer1-plugins-good
+
+On macOS (Homebrew)::
+
+  brew install gstreamer
+
+Building and Running
+********************
+
+.. zephyr-app-commands::
+   :zephyr-app: samples/subsys/mp/multicore
+   :board: mimxrt1170_evk/mimxrt1176/cm7
+   :goals: debug
+   :gen-args: -DmulticoreSHIELD=rk055hdmipi4ma0
+   :west-args: --sysbuild
+   :compact:
+
+On first run, the application mounts the SD card, creates ``test.mjpeg`` when needed,
+starts the eRPC-backed multicore pipeline, and waits for either EOS or an error from
+the sink side of the pipeline.
+
+Sample Output
+*************
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+   Remote started
+   [00:00:00.000,000] <inf> main: SDCard mounted at /SD:
+   [00:00:00.000,000] <inf> main: Created /SD:/test.mjpeg file for test (... bytes)
+   [00:00:xx.xxx,xxx] <inf> main: EOS message from element 6
